BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bucks Harbor
DTSTART:20260513T224500Z
DTEND:20260514T003500Z
DTSTAMP:20260513T224500Z
UID:W7Ppw7THGZ
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 98 mins (1h38m)\n\nIn the small port of Bucks Harbor
 \, its fishermen are shaped by brutal winters\, the ocean’s bounty\, and
  the emotional complexity of growing up in a community where a man’s wor
 th is often defined by the strength of his back.Director Peter Muller sche
 duled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/bucks-harbor\n\nAlso pla
 ying at:\n  • Uptown House 3 (Tue 12 May\, 5:30 PM)\n\nEstimated start: 
 15:55
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Three of a Kind
DTSTART:20260514T013000Z
DTEND:20260514T032000Z
DTSTAMP:20260514T013000Z
UID:x6oETmVrlZ
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 98 mins (1h38m)\n\nIn Charlotte Brodthagen’s tende
 r yet spiky debut feature\, a mother and daughter’s cozy Christmas is up
 ended when their estranged grandmother shows up at their cabin. Director C
 harlotte Brodthagen\, plus Producers Anne Falkesgaard and Sophie D'Souza\,
  scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/three-of-a-kind\n\n
 Also playing at:\n  • Uptown House 2 (Thu 14 May\, 3:30 PM)\n\nEstimated
  start: 18:40
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hijra
DTSTART:20260514T040000Z
DTEND:20260514T060500Z
DTSTAMP:20260514T040000Z
UID:oblCCYKExl
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 114 mins (1h54m)\n\nSitti is on a pilgrimage to Mecc
 a with her two rebellious granddaughters\, Sarah and Janna. But everything
  changes when one of the granddaughters goes missing.\n\nhttps://www.siff.
 net/festival/hijra\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Uptown House 1 (Thu 14 May\,
  12:30 PM)\n\nEstimated start: 21:10
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Burn
DTSTART:20260514T191500Z
DTEND:20260514T211000Z
DTSTAMP:20260514T191500Z
UID:Y7kMIUWd50
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 103 mins (1h43m)\n\nWhen runaway teen Ju-Ju is embra
 ced by a tribe of misfit youths in Kabukicho\, she finds belonging for the
  first time — until betrayal and despair twist her haven into a prison. 
 From the director of We Are Little Zombies.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festi
 val/burn\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Film Center (Tue 12 May\, 8:30 PM)\n\n
 Estimated start: 12:25
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
